**🎯 Functional Correctness** | **🟡 Minor** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Reject `/…/` regex anchors on K rows.**

A K row builds its keep-English token from `literal(anchor)`. If the anchor is written as `/…/`, the token pattern searches for the literal slash-delimited regex text, such as `/literal(?!ly)/`. Real `msgid` text never contains that string. As a result, `source_has` is always false, and the K-survival check never refuses anything for that token.

The self-test does not catch this case. `token_verdict` puts the same raw `token` string into its synthetic `msgid`, so the literal pattern matches its own spelling.

Refuse this combination at parse time so the gate cannot pass silently.

